Modified by MultiPak through 2026-11-18.

MultiPak uses a modified version of Waydroid 1.6.3. The changes allow several separate
Android containers, each with its own images, applications and data, network and shortcuts.
They also integrate Android with Linux: links, notifications, media controls, volume per
app, sending files and the choice of microphone and webcam. The Waydroid installed on the
system stays separate. How it works:
https://github.com/goulielmos-linux/multipak/blob/main/docs/howandroidcompatibilityworks.pt-BR.md

Credits: the separate containers follow the idea of Waydroid PR #1990
(https://github.com/waydroid/waydroid/pull/1990, not applied as a patch), and SELinux
labeling follows the Fedora Waydroid package (https://src.fedoraproject.org/rpms/waydroid).

